          <text x="150" y="104">ordinary</text><text x="150" y="120">waking mind</text>
          <text x="248" y="104">meditation ·</text><text x="248" y="120">flow · dream</text>
          <text x="316" y="104" fill="#9b7ddb">psychedelic</text><text x="316" y="120" fill="#9b7ddb">state</text>
        </g>
        <g stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width=".7"><path d="M60 80 v14 M180 80 v14 M280 80 v14 M340 80 v14"/></g>
        <g font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="10.5" fill="#c9bda3">
          <text x="40" y="180">Default mode network coherence falls as entropy rises.</text>
          <text x="40" y="200">The self-model loosens; priors lose their grip; novel</text>
          <text x="40" y="220">connections become cheap — and so does false certainty.</text>
          <text x="40" y="252" fill="#cf7f8d">Higher entropy is not automatically higher truth.</text>
          <text x="40" y="270" fill="#cf7f8d">It is higher plasticity. What you do with it matters.</text>
        </g>
